# ─── Large local artifacts (NEVER commit — GitHub rejects >100 MB files) ──────
# Darkeden/ is the live installed client (~1.8 GB), regenerated by
# PUBLISH_RELEASE.cmd. release_site/ is the generated update site (~1.8 GB),
# regenerated by MAKE_DARKEDEN_RELEASE.cmd. Both are build products.
# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live server configs carry DB_PASSWORD / UI_DB_PASSWORD / DIST_DB_PASSWORD
# in plaintext. Phase 8B (2026-08-06) shipped the fix -- `conf/*.conf.template`
# with ${DKRIX_*} placeholders, expanded by Properties::expandEnvVars
# (src/Core/Properties.cpp:46, wired in at :169) -- but stopped one step short:
# the real .conf files stayed tracked. They are untracked as of 2026-08-10 and
# ignored here so a stray `git add -A` cannot publish a live credential. The
# .template files remain tracked and are the reference copy.
dkrixserver/conf/*.conf
dkrixserver/docker/conf/*.conf
!dkrixserver/conf/*.conf.template
# The same stale credential also lives in the alternate host profile and in the
# local backup copies, which the rules above do not reach: `*.conf` does not
# match `.new`, and it does not cross a `/` into `backup/`. Untracked 2026-08-10
# alongside the set above. These are host-specific local copies with no template
# counterpart; `conf/*.conf.template` is the reference for all of them.
dkrixserver/conf/*.new
dkrixserver/conf/backup/
# docker/.env holds MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD and the DKRIX_* database passwords that
# docker-compose.yml interpolates. `.env.example` is the tracked reference copy
# and must stay free of real values.
.env
!.env.example

Darkeden/
# Darkeden-debug/ is the side-by-side runtime dir for the VS2022 Debug client
# used by the smoke test (debug binaries + a junction to Darkeden/Data). Local
# only — see docs/smoke-test/PORTING-NOTE.md, "STEP3 drift".
Darkeden-debug/
Darkeden__quarantine/
release_site/
*.rar
*.zip
*.7z

